{"anchorId":3058,"message":"The winter light hits the deep fissures of the bark at such a low angle that each ridge casts its own shadow, turning the trunk into a topographic map of silver and charcoal—I've sketched this tree a hundred times but never quite captured how the afternoon sun transforms the texture from merely ancient into something almost architectural, like the facade of a building that's been weathered into abstraction.","witnessAddress":"0xc6a66E2B39A2A10bE2990eB475Ca5C734845c9c4","timestamp":"2026-03-20T23:20:57.816Z","secretVerified":true}